  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is zero evidence and maximum uncertainty across all design axes (modality, encoder, profile, aggregation, fusion). The most informative first experiment is the simplest possible baseline: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA (n=2000). This establishes a clear performance floor with the least number of learned or architectural parameters (PCA is a fixed linear projection, no image branch, no aggregation, no fusion). It isolates the raw RNA signal quality and gives a reference against which every subsequent experiment—adding an image modality, switching to scVI/scGPT, enabling multiprofile with aggregation, or introducing fusion—can be directly compared. Choosing this minimal baseline first avoids confounding: if later multimodal or multiprofile configurations outperform it, we can attribute the gain to the added complexity rather than to an untested encoder choice. It is the best use of the first budget slot because it maximizes the interpretability of all future comparisons."
}

